# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
# 1. Copy it to a new file called .env in this same folder.
#    Windows: copy .env.example .env
# 2. Open .env and paste each key straight after its = sign.
#    No quotes, no spaces. Example:  GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_abc123
# 3. Save. Never commit .env. Git ignores it, and it holds your secrets.
#
# Every value here is optional. With no key, TradeMind still works.

# ---- AI explanations (optional) -------------------------------------------
# Without a key, each finding is explained by text the tool writes itself.
# With a key, a model rewords that text into friendlier sentences, and TradeMind checks the reply.
#
# How to get a free Groq key:
#   1. Go to https://console.groq.com and sign up (no card needed).
#   2. Open "API Keys" and press "Create API Key".
#   3. Copy the key (it starts with gsk_). It is shown once, so paste it below now.
# Then run:  uv run trademind analyse your-file.csv --explain groq
# Or start the web app with:  uv run trademind serve   (it uses Groq automatically when a key is set)
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Which Groq model to use. The default is fine. Free-tier limits are set per model.
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant

# ---- Running a model on your own computer (optional) ----------------------
# Instead of Groq, `--explain ollama` uses a model installed in Ollama. Nothing leaves your machine.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b

# ---- Web app --------------------------------------------------------------
# How many files one visitor can upload in an hour. 0 turns the limit off.
UPLOADS_PER_HOUR=10
